.TH BIGINTSUB 3 "2026-09-21" "BigNums" "Library Functions Manual"
.nr HY 0
.ds AD l
.SH NAME
bigIntSub, bigIntCmp \- subtract or compare unsigned big integers
.SH SYNOPSIS
.nf
.B #include \(dqbignums.h\(dq
.sp
.BI "int bigIntSub(BigInt *" "result" ", const BigInt *" "a" ","
.BI "    const BigInt *" "b" ");"
.sp
.BI "int bigIntCmp(const BigInt *" "a" ", const BigInt *" "b" ");"
.fi
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B bigIntCmp()
compares the canonical unsigned values a and b.
.B bigIntSub()
stores a minus b in result, provided a is at least b.
The destination may alias a, but must not alias a distinct b: the initial
copy of a would overwrite b before subtraction.
.SH RETURN VALUE
.B bigIntCmp()
returns \-1, 0, or 1 when a is less than, equal to, or greater than b.
.B bigIntSub()
returns 0 on success or \-1 when a is less than b.
In the latter case result is not modified.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR bigIntAddUInt_32 (3),
.BR bignums (3),
.BR bignums (7)
